      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Deficiency of pain perception may be at the origin of bone and/or joint lesions. In children, these lesions frequent give rise to surprising and misleading radiological images as a result of the usual lack of immobilization due to a delayed diagnosis. Alterations in bone structure at the metaphyses and corticoperiosteal ossifications can suggest malignant affections. Trauma is generally the predominant factor in the etiology of these lesions."},
